<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="fade-in">What we deliver</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
            <li class="fade-in">A responsive website or app that follows the design file exactly — typography, spacing, colour, motion</li>
            <li class="fade-in">Automated visual verification: screenshots of every view compared against the design before delivery</li>
            <li class="fade-in">Accessibility built in — WCAG as the floor, neuroinclusion as the ambition</li>
            <li class="fade-in">Performance: fast load times, optimised images, strong Lighthouse scores</li>
            <li class="fade-in">A CMS where needed (e.g. Umbraco) so content can be updated without a developer</li>
            <li class="fade-in">Clean, documented code anyone could take over</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="fade-in">How it works</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Handover</h3>
                <p>We take your design files (Figma, Sketch or XD), copy, images and any API documentation — and come back with a fixed quote and timeline.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Build</h3>
                <p>AI agents build under senior direction, view by view. You get rolling previews — no black boxes.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Visual verification</h3>
                <p>Playwright captures screenshots of every view at multiple screen sizes. They're compared against the design file until they match — that's what we mean by pixel-perfect.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Delivery</h3>
                <p>Deployment to your environment or your client's, with performance and accessibility checks as part of the handover.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

